description:
Read or change Jukka's single Nest thermostat. With no args, reads current state. With fields set, issues SDM commands in fixed order: mode → target_temperature → fan_mode → eco_enabled.

PRECONDITIONS (HTTP 400 if violated):
  - set_target_temperature requires HEAT or COOL — pass `mode` in the same call if currently OFF.
  - eco_enabled: true requires HEAT or COOL (cannot enable from OFF).
  - fan_mode currently only supports `on`; auto/off reject.
  - HEATCOOL mode not allowed (single-mode only).

Recipes:
  - Cool to 75F (works from OFF too):  {"mode": "COOL", "target_temperature": 75}
  - Heat to 68F:                        {"mode": "HEAT", "target_temperature": 68}
  - Change setpoint (must be in HEAT/COOL already): {"target_temperature": 72}
  - Turn off:                           {"mode": "OFF"}
  - Enable eco (must be in HEAT/COOL):  {"eco_enabled": true}
  - Kick fan on:                        {"fan_mode": "on"}
  - Read current state:                 {}

When in doubt about current mode, call {} first to read state.
